          "cos": 0.712
        }
      ],
      "a": "Volcanic ash can cause scratches to the eyes and lungs because it is made of small particles that are hard and prickly [1]. It can also enter deep into the lungs with the air, causing increased coughing, shortness of breath, runny nose, and throat pain [2]. People with asthma or bronchitis may experience coughing fits, a feeling of chest tightness, and labored breathing, so they should be careful [2]. People with serious heart conditions should also be cautious [2]. If volcanic ash gets into your eyes, rinse it with water instead of rubbing it, and wear glasses instead of contact lenses [2].",
